---
const cols = [
  { n: "01", h: "No single view",
    p: "One dashboard per zone. To learn who is under attack you open forty tabs, or you don't look at all." },
  { n: "02", h: "Answers take an afternoon",
    p: "\"Why is this site slow in Europe?\" has a GraphQL query behind it that nobody on the team is going to write." },
  { n: "03", h: "Changes are frightening",
    p: "A WAF rule on a client's production site, typed at five o'clock, with no preview of what it blocks and no way back." },
];
---
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="sc">The problem</span>
      <h2>Cloudflare's dashboard assumes one zone and one expert.</h2>
      <p>You have neither. You have forty zones across six clients and a support queue. <a href="/use-cases" style="color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">See what you'd ask instead →</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cols">
      {cols.map((c) => (
        <div class="col"><span class="n">{c.n}</span><h3>{c.h}</h3><p>{c.p}</p></div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
